<section>
  <section>
    <h2>Do images have a proper text alternative ?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Can images that convey information be replaced by their alt text?</li>
      <li>Are decorative images marked to be ignored?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Alt attribute:</h2>

    <pre><code is:raw data-trim>&lt;img alt="logo AnySurfer"/&gt;</code></pre>
    <pre><code is:raw data-trim>&lt;area alt="Belgium" /&gt;</code></pre>
    <pre><code is:raw data-trim>&lt;input type="image" alt="Submit" /&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Which alternative text?</h2>
    <p>Think about what info you would need if you couldn't see the image</p>
    <p>
      <a
        target="tweede"
        href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/images/decision-tree/">
        An alt decision tree
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Decorative or informative?</h2>
    <p>Depends on context</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/poubelles_banniere.png"
      alt="sacs poubelles dans la banière d'un article sur la propreté publique"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/poubelles_banniere.png"
      alt="sacs poubelles dans la banière d'un article sur la propreté publique"
    />
    <p>Decorative image (alt="")</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/poubelles_calendrier.png"
      alt="images de sacs poubelles de couleurs différentes dans un calendrier des collectes"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/poubelles_calendrier.png"
      alt="sacs poubelles de couleurs différentes dans un calendrier des collectes"
    />
    <p>Image contributes meaning (alt="yellow bag")</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/dechets_verts_alt_deco.png"
      alt="4 images de déchets verts accompagnés de texte (feuilles, branchages, ...)"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/dechets_verts_alt_deco.png"
      alt="4 images de déchets verts accompagnés de texte (feuilles, branchages, ...)"
    />
    <p>Decorative because redundant(alt="")</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/social_media_icons.png"
      alt="logos de 4 réseaux sociaux"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/social_media_icons.png"
      alt="logos de 4 réseaux sociaux"
    />
    <p>
      Clickable images, hence not decorative (alt="Facebook", alt="twitter" etc)
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>How to check ? With web developer extension</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Web developer extension > images > display alt attributes
        <img
          src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/webdev_display_alt.png"
          alt="extension web developer"
        />
      </li>
      <li>For decorative images we must have alt=""</li>
      <li>
        Only allows to test images inserted as img element in html code, not
        svg, icons, background images,...
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>How to check ? Inspect accessibility tree</h3>
    <p>
      <img
        src="https://images.anysurfer.be/alt/alt_sr_only_text_a11ytree.png"
        alt="Youtube icon link in a11y tree"
      />
    </p>
    <p>In the example, the name of the link is "Follow us on YouTube"</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>How to check ? Use screenreader</h3>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Images: points of attention</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Search button (magnifying glass) name is "search" (translated)</li>
      <li>Hamburger button name is "menu", not "toggle navigation"</li>
      <li>Social media icons name is for example "Facebook"</li>
      <li>Look at image in context and avoid redundancy</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
